1. Licensor and Scope of the Agreement

1.1. Melvad Limited Liability Company (https://melvad.com) grants the user of the SDK
(the Licensee) a non-exclusive license on the terms of this Agreement.

1.2. The Melvad SDK (the SDK) is a software development kit distributed
by the Licensor for iOS, Android, and Unity to integrate applications with
the Melvad advertising platform. This Agreement applies to each version
of the SDK supplied with this text, including the executable libraries,
interface files, and other software components of the Licensor included
in the kit. Section 4 governs third-party components.

1.3. This Agreement is entered into under the simplified procedure set
out in Article 1286(5) of the Civil Code of the Russian Federation.
After being given an opportunity to review the terms, the Licensee accepts
them by first integrating the SDK into an application project or running
the SDK for testing or operational use. Where integration is carried out
on behalf of an organization, its authorized representative accepts
the Agreement.

2. Permitted Uses

2.1. The Licensee may download and reproduce the SDK to the extent
necessary to store, integrate, build, test, and operate applications
that the Licensee publishes itself or is authorized by the application
owner to publish.

2.2. The Licensee may integrate the SDK through the interfaces specified
in its documentation, configure it, and include its executable components
in application builds. Standard application build, packaging, and signing
operations are permitted.

2.3. The Licensee may reproduce, distribute, and make the SDK available
to the public as part of an application, including a paid application,
through app stores and other lawful distribution channels. This permission
includes submitting builds to the operators of those channels for review,
listing, delivery, and updates. End users may run the SDK as part of
an application they have obtained in order to use the application's
features.

2.4. The Licensee may engage employees and contractors to work on
the application on its behalf and within the scope of the rights granted
under this Agreement. The Licensee is responsible for ensuring that they
comply with its terms.

2.5. The license is granted free of charge, worldwide, for the duration
of the exclusive right in the relevant version of the SDK, unless this
Agreement is terminated earlier under Section 6. Access to the Melvad
advertising platform and payments relating to advertising are governed
by separate agreements.

3. Restrictions

3.1. Without the Licensor's separate written consent, the Licensee may
not distribute the SDK or its components separately from an application,
including by publishing them in its own package registry, selling them,
sublicensing them, or including them in a third-party SDK, an app builder,
or another product for subsequent integration by third parties. The
